SOPA WORKING STEPS
SOPA is a true mess..follow these steps

1.Download the xenium dataset from 10x webpage or the links saved in STAT3D page
2.Extract the files and create a new folder called "sopa_directory" which must contain these files : experiment.xenium, morphology_mip and _focus, transcripts. parquest. Since it is not really clear which other files to include, I include them all except for morphology.ome.tiff
3.use conda and install sopa : pip install sopa[cellpose]
4.convert the sopa_directory in .zarr (SpatialData sdata) format : sopa convert sopa_directory --technology xenium # it is better to have this file ready before using the sopa environment which is described below
5.download the config.yaml file called "cellpose.yaml" , in the same folder where .zarr is located, the yaml file was modifed with the gpu addition and saved in test_sopa folder
6.close this prompt window and open a new one for creating the sopa environment
7.create the sopa environment with : conda update conda , followed by:  conda create --name sopa , then enter the env by writing: conda activate sopa #if u dont create the env the pipeline does not run
8.install snakemake : pip install snakemake
9.check if you need to install sopa, but it actually does not need : pip install sopa[cellpose]
10.from the env run  this command to enable parallelization of the processes : set SOPA_PARALLELIZATION_BACKEND=dask
11.run the pipeline with this command : snakemake --config sdata_path=C:/Users/Malin_Group/Kristi/sopa_directory.zarr --configfile=C:/Users/Malin_Group/Kristi/cellpose.yaml --cores 1 --use-conda


